# ELLSMS — excluded from the Docker build context (Phase 10, STEP 28).
#
# docker-compose.yml also bind-mounts the project root at runtime (./:/var/www/html), so this file
# only controls what gets baked into the IMAGE at build time, not what's visible inside a running
# container from that mount — this still matters for image size/hygiene and for anyone who ever
# builds without the bind mount (e.g. a registry-pushed image for a non-compose deployment).
.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.example
*.log
storage/logs/*
storage/benchmarks/*
storage/kyc/*
!storage/kyc/.gitkeep
# Runtime data under storage/ (uploads, exports, imports, backups, keys): it lives in the host
# checkout and reaches the containers through the bind mount, never through the image. Left in the
# build context it was sent to the Docker daemon on every build — backups and exports can be
# gigabytes — and storage/*.key would have been baked into the image.
storage/exports/*
!storage/exports/.gitkeep
storage/imports/*
!storage/imports/.gitkeep
storage/payment-receipts/*
!storage/payment-receipts/.gitkeep
storage/number-commitments/*
!storage/number-commitments/.gitkeep
storage/telegram-media/*
!storage/telegram-media/.gitkeep
storage/profile-documents/
storage/aimed-import/
storage/backups/
storage/rclone/
storage/*.key
storage/maintenance.flag
storage/dr-drill-status.json
# Uploaded landing videos and their posters (public/landing-videos.php): host data, same reasoning.
public/assets/video/landing/
public/assets/img/landing-video-posters/
# The other services' own build contexts; the PHP image never needs them.
smpp-bridge/
tg-worker/
tests/
docs/
PATHFINDER-2026-07-26/
graphify-out/
phpunit.xml
phpunit.integration.xml
vendor/
composer.lock
.phpunit.cache/
node_modules/
.claude/
